# Node sizes its heap from the machine's RAM, and the macOS CI runner lands
# near 2 GB — enough until v1.5.0, when Monaco and shiki pushed the renderer
# bundle past it and `electron-vite build` died with "Ineffective mark-compacts
# near heap limit". Windows and Linux build the same bundle and only survive
# because their runners have more RAM.
#
# This lives here rather than in .github/workflows/release.yml so it covers
# every build path at once — CI, `npm run build`, and a plain `npx electron-vite
# build` on a dev machine. npm injects it as NODE_OPTIONS into anything it
# spawns, npx included.
#
# It raises the ceiling; it does not reserve the memory.
node-options=--max-old-space-size=4096
